# Camera pod ("campod") -- Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W (512 MB), SD card. Role knobs
# consumed by build-image.sh + assemble-btrfs.sh. Same btrfs graph as every other
# role; only these knobs differ. See coordinator#96 "one btrfs layout, per-role
# knobs".
#
# Named campod, not pod: a bare "pod" is hopelessly aliased in a Kubernetes-
# adjacent environment, and these are camera pods specifically (arm-mounted or
# belly-mounted -- the mount point varies, the camera does not).

# @data is the capture volume, and this path is LOCKSTEP WITH THE COORDINATOR
# REPO. It has to equal coord_state_root in host/ansible/roles/campod, which
# creates {config,captures} on top of it.
#
# If the two diverge, @data is simply never mounted where anything writes, so
# captures land on @var: no error, no warning, and the power-loss properties the
# subvolume exists for silently stop applying. The only symptom is
# `findmnt /var/lib/campod` showing @var instead of @data.
#
# Changing it means changing both repos in one window.
DATA_MOUNT=/var/lib/campod

# SD medium: single metadata to halve write-amplification.
METADATA=single

# Serial console (enable_uart=1 + dtoverlay=disable-bt) and the dwc2 gadget-net
# overlay. See the file for why each line is there.
CONFIG_APPEND=roles/campod/config.append.txt

# Still NOT here: pps-gpio (no PPS is wired on this vehicle -- coordinator#211),
# and the dwc2/g_ether *module loading*, which is the ansible layer's job via
# /etc/modules-load.d/. The camera itself needs nothing -- the vendor default
# camera_auto_detect=1 covers it.

# Make the SERIAL port the primary console, not HDMI.
#
# The kernel sends printk to every console= device, but userspace /dev/console is
# the LAST one -- and that is where systemd writes its status output. The vendor
# cmdline lists serial first and tty1 second, which puts every systemd line on a
# monitor and leaves a serial capture showing raw printk only.
#
# So: drop the vendor's leading serial console and re-add it at the end. tty1 stays
# in the list, so HDMI still works as a fallback -- it is just no longer the one
# you must be plugged into. A pod in the field has a UART from the coordinator or
# a laptop; it does not have a monitor.
# Drop the graphics stack. A campod has no display of any kind: the payload is a
# camera and an accelerometer, and the only human interface is the serial console.
#
# CMA. A booted campod shows CmaTotal 262144 kB of MemTotal 425108 kB. That
# 256MB comes from device tree, not the kernel: the kernel is built with
# CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=5, and vc4-kms-v3d is the only loaded overlay the
# overlays README documents as controlling CMA.
#
# Which means removing the overlay REQUIRES setting CMA explicitly -- see
# roles/campod/config.append.txt. Without that line CMA falls to the kernel's
# 5MB, and the camera needs ~48 MiB, so the camera would stop working.
#
# 128MB is the largest value the overlays README does not gate on 1GB of RAM:
#   cma-256   CMA is 256MB (needs 1GB)
#   cma-128   CMA is 128MB
# This board has 512MB. The reservation is sized for different hardware.
#
# NO runtime-performance claim is attached to this. The region is not idle --
# the page allocator uses CMA for movable allocations when no client wants it --
# and shrinking it does not reduce migration work, because cma_alloc migrates
# the range it needs for a request rather than the region. What it does change
# is that 128MB stops being movable-only and becomes usable by slab, page tables
# and everything else that cannot live in CMA. Whether any of this moves the
# refault numbers is coordinator#316's open question, not this file's premise.
#
# The overlay is also the reason the ALSA SoC stack is loaded at all --
# snd_soc_core shows used_by=2, vc4 and snd_soc_hdmi_codec -- which is how HDMI
# audio reaches a board with no speaker. dtparam=audio=on adds snd_bcm2835,
# used_by=0.
#
# Kernel modules are resident, unswappable and unreclaimable, so this is the one
# category where removal returns memory outright. Measured on a booted campod:
# drm 700K, drm_kms_helper 224K, snd_soc_core 292K, snd_pcm 164K, snd 120K and
# the rest of the chain come to ~2.4 MiB, against 7.3 MiB of loaded modules in
# total. About a third of everything the kernel has loaded, for a display and a
# speaker this board does not have.
#
# camera_auto_detect is NOT removed -- that is the camera.
CONFIG_REMOVE="dtoverlay=vc4-kms-v3d* dtparam=audio=on display_auto_detect=*"

CMDLINE_REMOVE="console=serial0,*"
CMDLINE_APPEND="console=serial0,115200"
